# E3: the eight-seat quad EXACTNESS arm c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad-gate (E2 plus QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_SINGLES_AUDIT=all: every member of each batched group is drafted again on its own single-user capture with the
# same seed and compared bit for bit). The verifier checks every draft, so a wrong quad draft for seats 4-7 only lowers acceptance and no text comparison sees it; this audit does. Runs only if E2 attached
# (NEEDS in ORDER.txt). The audit costs time: never read E3 for speed.
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean, which requires at least one '[DRAFT-SINGLES-AUDIT] ... group=[0, 1, 2, 3] ... equal=1' line and one for group=[4, 5, 6, 7], no equal=0 line, both quads' engaged and pooled
# lines as in E2, and no stall. Per request accepted tokens and verify-round counts equal E1's and E2's. Duration (estimate): 120 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent8_code,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_steady,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
